16. Presentation of the Cheyenne Passenger Rail Station Site Selection
Study.
25 - 177
Christopher Yaney, director, Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization, presented
the MPO study of potential locations for a future passenger rail station.  The study was
done in partnership with the city of Cheyenne, with funding from the Wyoming
Department of Transportation.  The rail service would connect Cheyenne with Fort
Collins, Boulder, Denver, Colorado Springs, and beyond.  Yaney said the study found
the Old Happy Jack Road and Reed Avenue sites can both accommodate a
passenger rail station.  Continued study and engagement are required.
The report was received and filed.
