25. Consideration of a resolution giving public notice of Laramie County's
intent to adopt the 2025 Laramie County Land Use Regulations.
25 - 187
Resolution, Public Notice to adopt the 2025 Laramie
County Land Use Regulations
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said the resolution gives statutory notice of the county's intent
to adopt the 2025 Land Use Regulations and a 45-day public comment period on the
proposed changes to the regulations.  The Board of County Commissioners will
consider adopting the proposed regulations on July 1.
Chairman Malm acknowledged members of the public in attendance who wished to
comment on the proposed regulations.  He opened the meeting for PUBLIC
COMMENT.
Bonnie Burlando, Jennifer Stone, Keith Fogg, Benjamin Kramer, and Scott Butler
expressed concerns about infringement of property owners' rights, burdensome
permitting processes, fees, and zone changes.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.  He
encouraged residents to review the proposed regulations and said the board could
pass them in their entirety, in part, or not at all.  The proposed regulations are on the
Planning and Development website and persons can submit written comments online,
via email to Planning office or to the County Clerk.
