31. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a subdivision permit and plat for
Skyview Estates, 3rd Filing, Laramie County, WY.
25 - 185
Skyview Estates, 3rd Filing, Subdivision Permit and
Plat
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Jones Land Surveying, on behalf of various owners in the
Skyview Estates Subdivision, submitted a Subdivision Permit and Plat application to
replat portions of the Skyview Estates Subdivision, 2nd Filing, Laramie County, WY.
The application was submitted to consolidate many of the small lots, originally created
for airplane hangars, to make them larger and more buildable under current County
standards.
Arnold presented the staff report.  He said the applicant's intent is to consolidate 26
small lots, originally platted into 11 lots, to support larger hangars that people in the
current market wish to build.  He noted that the replatted lots would not be permitted
septic systems given their small size and a plat note clarifies they cannot be used as
residences under the AMEC memo.
Based on evidence provided, Arnold said staff recommends approval of the
subdivision permit and plat with no conditions and adoption of the findings of fact a
and b.
Chairman Malm opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT.  Patrice Gapen,
resident, spoke in favor of the item.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Heath, seconded by Commissioner
Hollingshead, to approve the Subdivision Permit and Plat for Skyview
Estates, 3rd Filing, with no conditions, and adopt the findings of fact a and
b.  The motion carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead,
Zwonitzer
Aye:
