### Page 12 of 14

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
May 6, 2025
is situated in the LU - Land Use Zone District. Under Laramie County Land Use
Regulations (LCLUR) § 2-2-133(d)(iv), the Planning and Development director may
require a site plan to have a public hearing before the Board of County
Commissioners if it is determined that the impacts of the proposed use will
significantly impact surrounding properties.
Arnold reported that Planning determined the proposed use is a permissible use
under LCLUR § 4-2-114(a). The use may not be denied, but commissioners may
direct Planning to place conditions upon the site plan to mitigate impacts to
surrounding neighbors.
Arnold presented the staff report and said the subject property is a 7.13-acre parcel
and current use is vacant residential land. The applicant wishes to construct a
barn-like structure, storage building, three cabins, and a parking lot. The project will
have two phases.
Based on evidence provided, Arnold said staff recommends approval with one
condition and adoption of findings of fact a and b of the staff report.
Chairman Malm opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT.  Residents Rick Bell,
Dustin Smith, Michael Smith, Brigitte Peters, Eric Wiles, Zakkary Keller, Dennis
Peters, Jill Brewer, Doris Carter, Steven Murray, and Thomas Kaetzer were among
those speaking in opposition to the project.  Bell said of the 74 lots in the subdivision,
54 residents signed a petition opposing the proposed business. Residents' concerns
included increased traffic and safety, road deterioration, pollution from traffic, lighting,
and noise, the need for fencing to screen the area, water usage, commercial activity in
residential neighborhood, impact on sewer system, effect on property values, and
emergency response times.
Chairman Malm and Vice Chairman Thompson pointed out that covenants are legal
agreements among landowners to protect neighborhoods.  However, the county is not
a party to the agreements and cannot take action on them.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.

A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thomson, seconded by
Commissioner Hollingshead, to approve the White Antelope Barn Site
Plan and to adopt the findings of fact a and b with the condition that all
agency comments must be addressed and corrections made to the site
plan before a certificate of review is issued.
A motion was made by Commissioner Zwonitzer, seconded by
Commissioner Hollingshead, to amend the motion to add the following
conditions:  1) North boundary of property is to be fenced 2) A traffic study
Page 12 of 14
```

### Page 13 of 14

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
May 6, 2025
is to be conducted 3) A map is to be submitted showing where natural
screening will be placed.
Malm, Heath, Hollingshead, Zwonitzer
Aye:
Thompson
Nay:
Vice Chairman Thompson explained his "no" vote on the additional conditions.  He
said the conditions were vague.  He said the only way to balance property owners and
neighbors' interests without being arbitrary and capricious was through land use
regulations, and the issue before the board was a use by right matter.  He said the
board does not have the ability to deny the project but can mitigate the effects on
neighbors through the site plan.
Commissioner Zwonitzer explained his intention to vote "no" on the project.  He said it
is someone's right to do what they want with their property; however, the project will
have significant impact on the surrounding residential area.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Hollingshead, to approve the White Antelope Barn Site
Plan and adopt the findings of fact a and b with the following conditions:
1) All agency comments must be addressed and corrections made to the
site plan before a certificate of review is issued; 2) North boundary of
property is to be fenced; 3) A traffic study is to be conducted; 4) A map is
to be submitted showing where natural screening will be placed.
 The motion carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead
Aye:
Zwonitzer
Nay:
The meeting adjourned at 5:52 p.m.
